§ `Rates`

-- Four assertions for the encoding skill's check.sh (skills/encoding-a-subject/assets/check.sh),
-- which counts them from the text of `l4 run`: the first three read a TYPICALLY default,
-- so each carries a NOTE line, which moves its message to the lines below `Message:`;
-- the fourth supplies the value with WITH and keeps its message on that line.
-- Counted as satisfied 3 and failed 1 (the failed one is the module's one error).

    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
          `the standard deduction` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 100

GIVETH A NUMBER
doubled MEANS `the rate` TIMES 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`net` MEANS 1000 MINUS `the standard deduction`

#ASSERT doubled EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `net` EQUALS 900
#ASSERT doubled EQUALS 7
#ASSERT (doubled WITH `the rate` IS 5) EQUALS 10
